# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# mitcad#1780: editing a feature whose stored pick is gone, on
# gone-pick-edit.json: Thread1's first face went when Extrude1 took another
# circle. The Faces chip says one of its two picks is missing, the panel's
# message names the input in words, the list of picks marks the gone one,
# and its ✕ takes it out: the edit then builds and OK keeps it. All
# geometry is synthetic.
# Run by tools/ui-gone-pick-edit-test.sh (Linux) and
# tools/ui-windows-gone-pick-edit-test.ps1 (Windows).
wait-idle
window-resize 1400 990
command view.fit
wait-idle
mark
dblclick-logged '^Timeline Thread1 at '
expect-log 'Editing F5 with Thread'
wait-log '^Preview Thread: failed' 30
wait-log '^Thread Faces: 1 of 2 pick[(]s[)] gone: face F2:side[(]c2[)] of F2[.]b0' 30
wait-log '^Panel Thread faces: 2 selected, 1 missing' 30
wait-log '^Panel Thread picks faces: 1[.] .* [(]missing[)]; 2[.] ' 30
wait-log '^Panel Thread error: A face of Faces is gone: pick it again' 30
wait-idle 30
screenshot '${MITCAD_TEST_WORK}/gone-pick-edit.png'
# The gone pick is the one chosen in the list: its ✕ takes it out.
mark
button '^✕$' remove_pick_faces
wait-log '^Thread Faces: 1 face' 30
wait-log '^Preview Thread: ok' 30
wait-idle 30
expect-no-log '^Panel Thread faces: [0-9]+ selected, [0-9]+ missing'
mark
button '^OK$'
expect-log 'Edited F5' 30
expect-never 'TestDriver: FAIL'
